{"text": "VIII\n\nam Maloney\n\nDonald J. Trump for President, Inc.\n\nRegional Political Director - Raleigh, NC: August - November 2016\nResponsible for southeastern NC under State Director, Jason Simmons. This title required\ngathering and facilitating volunteers, coordinating with state GOP staffers, managing events, and\ndriving office production. Mr. Maloney\u2019s region delivered 22 of 26 counties on Election Day.\n\nField Coordinator - Greenville, SC: October 2015 - February 2016\nCo-managed the Trump Greenville Campaign Office under the supervision of SC Field Director,\nJames Epley. Duties included operating phone banks, organizing volunteers, office management,\nand coordinating with staffers. Our office delivered all 15 counties in our region on primary day.\n\nField Coordinator - Fayetteville, NC: March 2016\n\nSupervised NC\u2019s first Trump Campaign office. Duties included operating phone banks and\norganizing volunteers.\n\nVolunteer - McLean, VA: March - August 2016\n\nServed at a phone bank and regional delegate convention for campaign under supervision of VA\n& MD Trump Field Director, John Jaggers.\n\nOther Political\nTrafalgar Group - Pendleton, SC: May - June 2016\n\nWas responsible for handling data, volunteers, and phone banks in Will Lewis\u2019 successful\nGreenville County Sheriff campaign.\n\nResearcher at Jackson Alvarez Group - Tysons, VA: January 2013 - October 2015\nResearcher for corporate and political clients. This position involved sieving large volumes of\nmedia and data to create substantive reports on business interests, current and potential\ninvestors, candidates, etc. Some past clients include:\ne North Carolina Governor, Pat McCrory\ne Colorado GOP (helped flip State House and Senate to GOP control)\n\ne Mississippi Lt. Governor, Tate Reeves\nGOP Volunteer - Various Campaigns\ne 2012: Republican National Convention Aide, Committee on events\n\ne 2014: Bruce Von Cannon for Congress, NC-6\n\ne 2015: Bill Janis for VA State Senate, Hal Parrish for VA State Senate\n\nAwards\nEagle Scout, Boy Scouts of America: 2008\n\nEducation\nChristopher Newport University - Newport News, VA: 2009-2013\n\nCompleted Bachelor of Arts Degree with a double major in communication studies and history\nwith a minor in leadership studies.",
"words": [
